                                        "type":  "organization",
                                        "description":  "The Maharashtra Surface Water Agency operates within the larger framework of the Maharashtra Water Resources Regulatory Authority (MWRRA), which oversees the state\u0027s water management and regulatory functions. The MWRRA, established in 2005, is responsible for ensuring the judicious, equitable, and sustainable use of the state\u0027s water resources, which includes managing surface water for irrigation, domestic use, and industry.\r\n\r\nThe state has a detailed water policy that emphasizes equitable water distribution, efficient usage, and the promotion of water conservation. The MWRRA also plays a significant role in regulating surface water distribution, managing water allocation for various sectors, and handling disputes regarding water resources. Key areas include controlling over-extraction, promoting water-use efficiency, and integrating sustainable practices across the state.\r\n\r\nMaharashtra\u0027s surface water management includes extensive infrastructure, such as dams and reservoirs, for storing water. The agency ensur",
